      en: "Rusape is a town in Manicaland province, Zimbabwe, with a population of around 30,000 (2012). Located on the Rusape River, it serves as an agricultural hub, with maize, tobacco, and cotton as main crops. The town was established in the 1890s as a trading post. It has a railway station on the Mutare-Harare line. The local economy is driven by agriculture and small-scale gold mining. The climate is temperate, with annual rainfall between 800-1000 mm. The nearby Bvumba Mountains offer scenic views and hiking trails, attracting tourists. The area also has forestry and timber production.",
